1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,150
In the last lesson, you designed an email.

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:04,348
Now let's send one!

3
00:00:04,348 --> 00:00:09,143
You'll choose exactly who gets it, write
a subject line people want to open,

4
00:00:09,143 --> 00:00:11,604
schedule it, and then read the results.

5
00:00:12,454 --> 00:00:17,373
Here in Marketing, Emails, we have a
draft ready to go: the November check-up

6
00:00:17,373 --> 00:00:17,948
reminder.

7
00:00:17,948 --> 00:00:21,271
Click it to open the builder,
give it one last look,

8
00:00:21,271 --> 00:00:24,210
then click Send or
schedule in the top corner.

9
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:26,574
Step one is recipients.

10
00:00:26,574 --> 00:00:31,314
You can send to all contacts, a smart
list, or anyone with certain tags.

11
00:00:31,314 --> 00:00:35,659
This reminder is only for patients
due a check-up, so choose Tags,

12
00:00:35,659 --> 00:00:36,844
and pick check-up.

13
00:00:36,844 --> 00:00:39,544
Kyntlo shows you how many people that is.

14
00:00:40,394 --> 00:00:42,167
Notice the note underneath.

15
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:46,566
Anyone who unsubscribed, or has
email turned off in Do Not Disturb,

16
00:00:46,566 --> 00:00:48,207
is skipped automatically.

17
00:00:48,207 --> 00:00:51,950
You never have to clean the
list by hand before you send.

18
00:00:52,798 --> 00:00:54,326
Step two is the sender.

19
00:00:54,326 --> 00:00:57,846
Use a name people recognise,
like your business name,

20
00:00:57,846 --> 00:01:00,502
and an email address on your own domain.

21
00:01:00,502 --> 00:01:05,484
The green badge means your dedicated
sending domain is set up and verified.

22
00:01:05,484 --> 00:01:08,672
We'll cover why that
matters in the next lesson.

23
00:01:09,522 --> 00:01:11,614
Step three is your subject line.

24
00:01:11,614 --> 00:01:13,379
Keep it short and personal.

25
00:01:13,379 --> 00:01:16,909
Type it, then add the first
name merge field in front.

26
00:01:16,909 --> 00:01:22,138
The preview text is the grey line people
see next to the subject in their inbox.

27
00:01:22,138 --> 00:01:24,688
Use it to give one more reason to open.

28
00:01:25,538 --> 00:01:28,613
Always send yourself a
test before the real thing.

29
00:01:28,613 --> 00:01:32,857
Click Send test email, then check
it on your phone and your computer.

30
00:01:32,857 --> 00:01:37,593
Look for typos, broken links, and make
sure the first name fills in properly.

31
00:01:38,442 --> 00:01:39,935
Step 4: when to send.

32
00:01:39,935 --> 00:01:42,209
Send now goes out straight away.

33
00:01:42,209 --> 00:01:47,042
Schedule lets you pick a date and
time, in your account's time zone.

34
00:01:47,042 --> 00:01:50,027
Let's choose Tuesday 3 November, at 10:00.

35
00:01:50,878 --> 00:01:53,726
For big lists, there's
also Send in batches.

36
00:01:53,726 --> 00:01:58,257
Kyntlo sends a set number of emails,
waits, then sends the next group.

37
00:01:58,257 --> 00:02:00,846
It's gentler on your sending reputation.

38
00:02:00,846 --> 00:02:03,111
You'll use this in the next lesson.

39
00:02:03,961 --> 00:02:05,198
Now click Schedule.

40
00:02:05,198 --> 00:02:10,276
Kyntlo shows a quick summary: the campaign,
how many people, and exactly when.

41
00:02:10,276 --> 00:02:11,903
Confirm, and you're done.

42
00:02:11,903 --> 00:02:15,093
Your campaign now shows
as scheduled in the list.

43
00:02:15,942 --> 00:02:19,648
Once a campaign has gone out,
click it to see the results.

44
00:02:19,648 --> 00:02:22,716
Delivered, opened and
clicked are the big three.

45
00:02:22,716 --> 00:02:26,614
Open rates are estimates, because
some email apps hide opens,

46
00:02:26,614 --> 00:02:29,745
so clicks are the most
reliable sign of interest.

47
00:02:30,595 --> 00:02:33,347
Link activity shows which
links people clicked,

48
00:02:33,347 --> 00:02:35,630
so you know what caught their interest.

49
00:02:35,630 --> 00:02:39,435
And the recipients list shows who
did what, one person at a time.

50
00:02:39,435 --> 00:02:42,128
Someone who clicked to
book but didn't finish?

51
00:02:42,128 --> 00:02:44,001
That's a perfect person to call.

52
00:02:44,852 --> 00:02:45,852
Here's a pro tip.

53
00:02:45,852 --> 00:02:48,617
The best time to send
depends on your audience.

54
00:02:48,617 --> 00:02:52,323
Try a weekday morning one month,
and an early evening the next.

55
00:02:52,323 --> 00:02:55,323
Compare the click rates,
and stick with the winner.

56
00:02:56,171 --> 00:02:58,135
You've sent your first campaign!

57
00:02:58,135 --> 00:03:02,800
Next, we'll make sure your emails land
in the inbox and not the spam folder,

58
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:05,255
with a few simple deliverability basics.

59
00:03:05,255 --> 00:03:06,114
See you there.
